{"name":"Sociable","hex":"#cf8c76","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sociable","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to socialize or be social.","Offering opportunities for conversation; characterized by much conversation."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sociable person.","A four-wheeled open carriage with seats facing each other."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sociable"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sociable","blocks":[{"text":"The sociable or buddy bike or side by side bicycle is a bicycle that supports two riders who sit next to one another, in contrast to a tandem bicycle, where the riders sit fore and aft. The name \"sociable\" alludes to its historic use for 2-person side-by-side tricycles and the relative ease with which the two cyclists can speak with each other, unlike on the tandem."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Btv1b8433329b-p103_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Btv1b8433329b-p103_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sociable","wikidata":"Q1973340"},{"title":"Sociable (carriage)","blocks":[{"text":"A sociable is an open four-wheeled carriage with face-to-face seating and folding hoods, used primarily as a light town or pleasure vehicle. The term originated in the 18th century and was applied to a variety of related forms as carriage design evolved, ranging from early phaeton-like bodies to later combinations of the Barouche and Victoria. Despite these variations, sociables share a common layout of face-to-face seating in an open body mounted on a light undercarriage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-10103%2C_Englisches_K%C3%B6nigspaar_bei_einem_Ausflug.jpg/330px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-10103%2C_Englisches_K%C3%B6nigspaar_bei_einem_Ausflug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sociable_(carriage)","wikidata":"Q7550397"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Sociable_1.jpg/330px-Sociable_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Sociable_1.jpg/330px-Sociable_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two people riding a sociable","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASociable_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Man_and_woman_on_a_Malvern_Star_abreast_tandem_bicycle%2C_c._1930s%2C_by_Sam_Hood.jpg/500px-Man_and_woman_on_a_Malvern_Star_abreast_tandem_bicycle%2C_c._1930s%2C_by_Sam_Hood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Man_and_woman_on_a_Malvern_Star_abreast_tandem_bicycle%2C_c._1930s%2C_by_Sam_Hood.jpg/500px-Man_and_woman_on_a_Malvern_Star_abreast_tandem_bicycle%2C_c._1930s%2C_by_Sam_Hood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Malvern Star sociable from the 1930s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan_and_woman_on_a_Malvern_Star_abreast_tandem_bicycle%2C_c._1930s%2C_by_Sam_Hood.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sociable_vis-a-vis_%283292137762%29.jpg/500px-Sociable_vis-a-vis_%283292137762%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sociable_vis-a-vis_%283292137762%29.jpg/1280px-Sociable_vis-a-vis_%283292137762%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sociable_vis-a-vis_%283292137762%29.jpg/500px-Sociable_vis-a-vis_%283292137762%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail